# Prismic Slices

- Type each slice with `SliceComponentProps<Content.XSlice>` and export the props type near the component.
- Keep `data-slice-type` and `data-slice-variation` on the root slice wrapper so Slice Machine metadata stays intact.
- Use `Bounded` as the default section wrapper unless the slice intentionally owns full-bleed layout.
- Use Prismic helpers like `isFilled`, `PrismicRichText`, `PrismicNextImage`, and `PrismicNextLink` instead of manually reading rich text, image, or link internals.
- Treat Prismic fields as nullable. Render optional fields only when filled instead of coercing empty values into UI.
- Do not rename generated custom type or slice model files unless the Slice Machine schema is updated too.
- Keep async Prismic queries in Server Components. Move animated or interactive parts into small Client Components.

```tsx
export type HeroProps = SliceComponentProps<Content.HeroSlice>;

const Hero: FC<HeroProps> = ({ slice }) => (
  <Bounded data-slice-type={slice.slice_type} data-slice-variation={slice.variation}>
    {/* slice UI */}
  </Bounded>
);
```
